{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1175829-apportation-sojourner","id":1175829,"title":"Apportation & Sojourner","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-13T13:09:08-08:00","id":1175829,"title":"Apportation & Sojourner","content":"Neither of these merits seem to be written to require line of sight to the destination, and in the case of the latter, it even seems implied that it wouldn't be required.<br /> Neither of them seem to require that the target space be unoccupied, either.<br /> <br /> Would you allow either of these merits to allow the user to move an object or person into space occupied by another object (into the ground, for example, or even just onto a busy street with people consistently walking by), either intentionally or by accident?<br /> <br /> If so, how would you adjudicate the damage or other effects of doing so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T23:33:39-08:00","id":1175921,"title":"","content":"I'd say not into an object but into the path of something? Sure. If it had a way of interacting with popping into an object I feel it'd have rules (likely damage) in the description. However, if you apporate in front of a car well, unless you get out of the way the car will hit you and damage you as normal. For someone teleported into this maybe, a single action would be allowed in their reaction. Like Dex + Athletics to dive away but not simply using their speed value or another power/ability, they might possess that could work fast enough.<br /> <br /> That, however, is just an off the cuff ruling, I cannot say it is the closest to RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}